---
import CommunityCardPreview from "../community/CommunityCardPreview.astro";
import ProfileViewPreview from "../ProfileViewPreview.astro";
import { useTranslations } from "../../i18n/utils";
import type { Lang } from "../../i18n/utils";
interface Props { lang?: Lang }
const { lang = "en" } = Astro.props;
const t = useTranslations(lang);
---
  <div class="form-section" data-section="preview" role="tabpanel" id="panel-preview" aria-labelledby="tab-preview">
    {
      /* The Preview tab. Both representations sit here together so
      they are comparable, and so the form itself stays a form.

      The profile page comes first: it is the artefact the member is actually
      building. The directory card is the smaller, secondary view of the same
      data — the image card itself, carousel and all, bound by
      renderCardPreview(), which is what /community renders since the directory
      switched over.

      NOTHING BETWEEN THEM BUT A RULE (2026-09-02, Josh: "make the preview be
      exactly the profile page seperated only by horizontal bars"). The two
      "YOUR PROFILE PAGE" / "YOUR DIRECTORY CARD" headings are gone with the
      preview's sheet and note. They were the editor naming its own contents
      over renderings that name themselves — a page with the member's name at
      the top of it, and a card with their name on it — and a label above a
      preview is one more thing between the member and the thing they are
      looking at. ProfileViewPreview draws the rule above and below itself;
      this section closes the last one under the card.

      THE CARD IS NAMED AGAIN (2026-09-26, Josh: "in the preview clearly
      label the gallery card!"). The page names itself; a lone card under
      it did not say where it goes, and read as one more work at the page's
      foot. So the card, and only the card, has a label and one line saying
      where it appears. */
    }
    <div class="preview-section">
      <ProfileViewPreview lang={lang} />
      <div class="preview-card">
        <div class="preview-card-head">
          <p class="label">{t("profile.preview.card")}</p>
          <p class="field-note">{t("profile.preview.cardNote")}</p>
        </div>
        <CommunityCardPreview />
      </div>
      <hr class="preview-rule" />
    </div>
  </div>
